  "states": [
    {
      "name": "populated",
      "file": "populated.html",
      "variant": "the ref's own data: build/F3 from docs/ui/fixture/trace.json (node, verdicts, findings, decisions). Gaps drawn as gaps: task rows, the A1 red-test commit, the TDD trailer and agent of the fix commits, per-verdict findings, the Agent trailer against the hook."
    },
    {
      "name": "in-flight",
      "file": "in-flight.html",
      "variant": "build/F6 after its first 20 loop events, cut from its loop.jsonl; not the ref's state. Title, rules, PR and dependencies are not in the cut and are drawn as gaps."
    },
    {
      "name": "incomplete",
      "file": "incomplete.html",
      "variant": "labelled placeholder: the completeness-banner incomplete snippet exactly as the stylekit has it, attached to no real node, because no node is TRAIL INCOMPLETE at this ref; every other region empty."
    },
    {
      "name": "git-only",
      "file": "git-only.html",
      "variant": "build/F0a, which predates the trail: git and trailers only."
    },
    {
      "name": "disagreement",
      "file": "disagreement.html",
      "variant": "build/F4 sign-off: the loop log's signoff event (4ea2ae8, line 51) against docs/qa/build-F4.md (43f38b6); only those two sources are in the data."
    }
